  "details": "I feel a lot of what makes VR experiences feel higher quality and more immersive is the smaller repetitive details. I was thinking if (for example) hopping through a portal had a cleaner transition rather than the world fading and music cutting out a few times when loading to another world, and instead playing a sort of \"teleporting\" effect (which I suppose could be toggled for those with motion sickness/epilepsy if needed) to hide some of the chunky loading steps and make world loading feel more seamless could be a neat QOL feature to implement. Of course there's more important things to implement first but, just food for thought! ;)",
